# 🎬 StreamBox — Streaming UI Prototype

A front-end streaming interface project built with **HTML, CSS, and JavaScript**, designed to simulate content discovery and navigation patterns commonly used in streaming platforms and connected TV applications. This project demonstrates grid-based layouts, client-side data rendering, keyboard navigation, and detail views without using frameworks.

---

## 📁 Project File Structure

streaming-content/
│
├── index.html # Application layout and UI structure
├── styles.css # Styling and layout (Grid, Flexbox)
├── script.js # Client-side application logic
│
├── images/ # Thumbnails and fallback assets
│
├── data/
│ └── shows.json # Content metadata source


---

## 🧩 Application Overview

### 🏠 `index.html`

* Main entry point of the application
* Defines the page layout, header, search input, genre filter, and content grid
* Loads styles and application logic

---

### ⚙️ `script.js`

* Fetches content from `data/shows.json`
* Dynamically renders show cards
* Implements search and genre filtering
* Handles keyboard navigation using arrow keys and Enter
* Manages focus state and selection highlighting
* Controls the full-screen detail view overlay

---

### 🎨 `styles.css`

* Centralized styling for the application
* Grid-based layout for content discovery
* Focus and hover states for keyboard navigation
* Responsive design using CSS Grid and Flexbox
* Full-screen detail view styling

---

### 🗂️ `data/shows.json`

* Stores streaming content metadata
* Acts as the single source of truth for displayed content
* Includes title, genre, rating, year, and thumbnail path

---

## ⚙️ Core Functionality

* Fetches and renders streaming content from a local JSON data source
* Displays content in a responsive, grid-based layout
* Filters content by genre
* Supports title-based search
* Implements keyboard navigation for remote-style interaction
* Opens a full-screen detail view for selected content
* Handles loading states, missing content, and image errors

---

## 📺 Streaming-Oriented Design

* Keyboard-first navigation modeled after connected TV interfaces
* Focus management using visual highlighting and programmatic focus
* Grid-based content discovery patterns
* Separation of data, logic, and presentation
* Client-side rendering using vanilla JavaScript and the Fetch API

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

* HTML5
* CSS3 (CSS Grid, Flexbox)
* JavaScript (ES6)
* Fetch API
* Local JSON data

---

## ▶️ Running the Application

Because the application loads JSON using the Fetch API, it must be served through a local web server.

### VS Code (Recommended)

1. Install **Live Server**
2. Open `index.html` with Live Server
3. Open the provided local URL in a browser

---

## 📝 Notes

* Opening `index.html` directly in a browser may prevent JSON data from loading due to browser security restrictions
* The layout adapts automatically to screen size changes

---

## 🎯 Project Purpose

This project was created to:

* Demonstrate client-side scripting in a streaming application context
* Showcase UI patterns used in content discovery platforms
* Implement keyboard / remote-style navigation
* Render data-driven interfaces without frameworks

